;; Publication record of the static browser bundle web/ (JUN-346). It lives
;; here, next to kumitate.wasm.publication.edn, and not in web/: a file inside
;; web/ would change the CID it records.
;;
;; The CID is the UnixFS directory of the 5 files in web/ exactly as committed
;; (source commit below). Anyone holding the files re-derives it without a node
;; or a network:
;;
;;   ipfs add -r -Q --only-hash --cid-version=1 --raw-leaves --chunker=size-262144 web
;;
;; (Kubo 0.41.0. These flags are Kubo's defaults for --cid-version=1, so the
;; plain `ipfs add -r -Q --only-hash --cid-version=1 web` gives the same CID;
;; the balanced layout and sha2-256 are defaults too, and 5 entries are far
;; below the HAMT threshold.) Each file's sha256 is below; kumitate.wasm.js
;; carries the module whose sha256 kumitate.wasm.publication.edn records, and
;; the page checks it before running it.
;;
;; Routes (root ADR-2609092600, ADR-2609109200; owner 2026-10-22, confirmed for
;; kumitate 2026-10-23):
;;   primary    ipfs://{cid} below
;;   naming     ipns://{k51} - on hold by owner decision; no key was made
;;   secondary  https://kumitate.itonami.app/ through DNSLink - blocked on
;;              JUN-324 (registrar, DNS/DNSSEC, ingress/TLS); no record exists
